From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:01:21 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 101/162] hjviewer: the phone session's gesture guide and file
 transfer switch (TV-W7)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TV37: on a phone or tablet the gesture panel opens by itself once per mode,
a second after the first image of a remote screen session to a peer that is
not Android, with control, the soft keyboard closed and the Wayland keyboard
prompt answered. It carries a title row with [알겠습니다]; closing it ([알겠습
니다], the ▼ button, the mode button) marks the modes it showed as seen on
this device (hjv-gesture-seen-mouse, hjv-gesture-seen-touch); a panel left
open when the session ends marks nothing. The list says what HJViewer's
input does: in mouse mode a two-finger tap right-clicks and one finger
moves the pointer; no "canvas" words. The long press stays as it is (D-15).

TV39: 더 보기 has [파일 전송] first. It asks F1, then closes the remote
screen and opens the same PC's file transfer only once the page's close is
done (the phone's pages share gFFI and one session ID), within 10 s, else a
toast. The file screen has [원격 화면으로] beside its close button (F2 while
transfers are open) and switches back the same way; its dispose now waits
for gFFI.close(). The new session carries the old one's connection token,
so a permanent password typed by hand is not asked again. No hold of the
이용 비밀번호 ticket (D-14): F1 says that an app without a login enters it
again, and that a PC not in 내 PC may ask for its password or acceptance;
내 PC switches without a password. No Rust or bridge change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
